kroneckerIndices -- data which classify a matrix pencil up to strict equivalence
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (L, dualL, d) = kroneckerIndices(P,x,y)
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a matrix of linear forms
      * x, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,
      * y, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, degrees of minimal generators of
        the kernel
      * dualL, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, degrees of minimal generators
        of the kernel of the dual
      * d, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, elementary divisors

Description
===========

This function gives data which classify a matrix pencil up to strict
equivalence.  That is, these data determine the Kronecker normal form of the
pencil, up to rearranging the blocks.
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y]                                              |
|                                                                  |
|o1 = R                                                            |
|                                                                  |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = matrix{{x,y,x,y},{y,x,y,x},{x,y,x,y},{y,y,y,y},{x,x,y,y}}|
|                                                                  |
|o2 = | x y x y |                                                  |
|     | y x y x |                                                  |
|     | x y x y |                                                  |
|     | y y y y |                                                  |
|     | x x y y |                                                  |
|                                                                  |
|             5      4                                             |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : kroneckerNormalForm(A, ChangeMatrix => {false,false})        |
|                                                                  |
|o3 = | 0 0 0   0   |                                              |
|     | 0 x 0   0   |                                              |
|     | 0 y 0   0   |                                              |
|     | 0 0 x-y 0   |                                              |
|     | 0 0 0   x-y |                                              |
|                                                                  |
|             5      4                                             |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : kroneckerIndices(A,x,y)                                      |
|                                                                  |
|o4 = ({0}, {0, 1}, {x - y, x - y})                                |
|                                                                  |
|o4 : Sequence                                                     |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

