kroneckerNormalForm(Matrix,Matrix) -- normal form of a pair of matrices of scalars
**********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note kroneckerNormalForm: kroneckerNormalForm,
  * Usage: 
        (A',B',P,Q) = kroneckerNormalForm(A,B)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,
      * B, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note ChangeMatrix: kroneckerNormalForm, => ..., default value {true,
        true}, Kronecker normal form of a matrix of linear forms
  * Outputs:
      * A', a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,
      * B', a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,
      * P, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,
      * Q, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,

Description
===========

This function gives the normal form of a pair of matrices (A,B) over a field of
the same dimensions up to multiplication on either side by an invertible
matrix.  The return values are such that P*A*Q=A' and P*B*Q=B'.
