rationalNormalForm -- rational normal form of a matrix
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (B,P,Q) = rationalNormalForm A
        (B,P) = rationalNormalForm(A,ChangeMatrix=>{true,false})
        (B,Q) = rationalNormalForm(A,ChangeMatrix=>{false,true})
        B = rationalNormalForm(A,ChangeMatrix=>{false,false})
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a square matrix with constant
        entries
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * ChangeMatrix => ..., default value {true, true}
  * Outputs:
      * B, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the rational normal form of A
      * P, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, invertible (left) change of
        basis matrix
      * Q, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, invertible (right) change of
        basis matrix

Description
===========

This function produces a matrix B in rational normal form, and invertible
matrices P and Q such that P*Q = I and B = P*A*Q.
